  "slug": "sequences-promoter-38cf",
  "summary": "A new AF3 benchmark shows accuracy drops on novel RNAs, while probing-to-structure and cryoEM identification resources support experimental cross-checking.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how far deep-learning RNA and protein-RNA predictions can be trusted against experimental data. An AlphaFold 3 evaluation across more than 1,300 protein-RNA complexes and about 270 RNA-only systems reports that fold and interface accuracy decline for novel RNAs, framing generalization as the central limitation. Ribocentre-FoldBridge links nucleotide-resolved chemical probing profiles, in vitro and in cells, to X-ray and cryoEM 3D models, providing a route to check structures against experimental evidence. CryoID2 addresses a related but distinct task: a 3D U-Net predicts features from cryoEM maps and ranks protein and RNA candidates from a user pool. Together they emphasize reliability assessment and experimental grounding over model generation alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
